{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/general-onyx-path-discussion/storypath-system/1542892-storypath-ultra-advancement-is-surprisingly-fast","id":1542892,"title":"Storypath Ultra advancement is surprisingly fast","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","General Onyx Path Discussion","Storypath System"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-29T22:05:53-07:00","id":1542892,"title":"Storypath Ultra advancement is surprisingly fast","content":"Storypath Ultra recommends giving ~4 XP per session. A Skill dot costs 3 XP, an Edge dot 4 XP, and an Attribute or Power dot 5 XP. That means a player can reasonably expect to buy a dot in <i>any</i> trait in the system after each session, on average. One Skill dot + one Attribute dot = 2 sessions' worth of XP.<br /> <br /> Contrast with Scion, which recommends giving ~5 XP per session; in that game, Skill and Birthright dots cost 5 XP each, while Attribute dots and Knacks cost 10 XP each. So you can expect to improve a Skill or Birthright in one session, but improving an Attribute or getting a new Knack will take two. I'm assuming that Scion Knacks are equivalent to Power dots in Storypath Ultra.<br /> <br /> The question I have isn't so much the relative costs of the traits; it's the absolute rate of XP gain. With the stated rewards, I would expect 4 XP to be the <i>minimum</i> reward from a session, not the average. It's very easy to spend Momentum so the &quot;spend half the Momentum pool&quot; XP award will come in once every other scene - one scene to build the pool up, the next draws it down. Combine that with the short-term aspiration award and the &quot;make progress in the story&quot; award, and it'd be hard <i>not</i> to hit 4 XP. The more generous rewards in Scion make 5 XP the practical minimum per session in that game ... but in Scion that's just enough for one Skill dot, and in Storypath Ultra it buys 4/3 of a Skill dot. Advancement is 33% faster in the Ultra rules.<br /> <br /> So... are those the right numbers? Are Storypath Ultra characters meant to advance that much faster?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T23:52:11-07:00","id":1542895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/general-onyx-path-discussion/storypath-system/1542892-storypath-ultra-advancement-is-surprisingly-fast#post1542892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... are those the right numbers? Are Storypath Ultra characters meant to advance that much faster?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's called 'Ultra' not without reason. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( It's that fast. )<br /> <br /> On more serious note - I run <b>Trinity Continuum</b> 2E on <b>Storypath 'Classic' </b>(1E) - most of my session ends per 4 XP per player. ( Often more. ) Traits costs there are almost the same in Ultra. But players do not buy Skills or Edges, just hoarding XP for new Psi levels ( Legend equivalents in TC. ) Difference is that in <b>TC</b> 2E you BUY Psi, not given by story arcs milestones like in <b>Scion</b> 2E. We will see how it will play in <b>Curseborne </b>in couple of days...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T09:00:31-07:00","id":1542911,"title":"","content":"The costs in TC are 5 per Skill dot, 10 per attribute (equal to Scion), 2-3 per edge dot.<br /> Talents have a 4-5 per gift and 10 per facet dot<br /> Psions have 6-8 per mode dot, 12 per Psi<br /> Psiads have 8-10 per mode dot and 15 per psi dot<br /> Novas have 12 per nova trait dot and 16 per Quantum dot.<br /> <br /> So it\u2019s far slower than SPU, specially when dealing with powers, as you need to buy the power trait too.<br /> <br /> It is not bad to gain a skill, edge or power every session, and 1 attribute or power source every other session. I mean, if you are planning to go from zero to hero. But for a long campaign you end up in the top tear of the setting quite fast (specially Psions, that have little space for horizontal development).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}